In facet_strips.wrap, I think you need to check that the labels_df
data structure is being correctly formed when you run the llply(). I'd
start by inserting browser() right above that line, and try comparing
the results of your modified code with the results of the original
code.

I think the 'labels' passed to ggstrip need to be expressions (or
strings, if you don't want to parse them). For example, this code
would convert the labels to expressions which could then be passed to
ggstrip:
  parse(text = as.character(labels_df[[1]]))

Unfortunately there's no document that explains how ggplot2 works - if
you look at plot_build and plot_render, that will help to understand
the process.

-Winston

